{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MgV6dBDbTYi5qT7GWtcBCA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the research project carefully to define three tiers of Dream simulation scenarios.\n\nKey facts from the data:\n\n**Function-level results (complete, multi-seed):**\n- CLS (Qwen3-4B): mean acc 88.41% ± 0.96\n- CWM (Qwen3-4B): seeds show ~87.0-87.6% acc, exact match ~84%\n- TRAJ (Qwen3-4B): seeds show 85.66-87.40% acc\n- CLS 8B: 88.31-90.48% across seeds\n\n\n- CWM 8B: 86.24-87.67% across seeds\n\nLooking at the statistical comparison between CLS and CWM, the TOST equivalence test shows significance at the ±2pp margin (p=0.007), though the pooled gap is minimal at -0.45pp with a confidence interval spanning zero. DeepSeek models show more variability across seeds, with CLS ranging from 86.77-86.93%, CWM from 85.77-87.88%, and TRAJ starting at 83.24-85.08%.\n\nFor the repo-level experiments, Qwen3's CLS models achieved 83.63% on the 4B variant and around 84.79-85.60% on 8B across different checkpoints, with one seed reaching 87.92% on validation. The CWM approach struggled significantly with high unparseable rates across versions. DeepSeek's repo-level runs encountered multiple failures in the CLS pipeline, while the CWM training completed but had evaluation issues.\n\nLooking at the trajectory results, DeepSeek achieved 75-81.25% across different seeds on a smaller test set. I'm tracking several pending experiments including DeepSeek's v5 CLS run and additional evaluations. The zero-shot baselines show Qwen3 performing better than DeepSeek on both function and repo-level tasks, with function-level reaching 68.73% versus 63.02%. An oracle ensemble hit 90.63%, suggesting meaningful error complementarity exists between models, with block correlation showing a design effect around 4.\n\nThe re-repair attempts both failed, and the LLM judge results were mixed—the 8B model only reached 64.4% while the 32B improved to 71.69%. The real question now is whether DeepSeek's repo-level CLS will finally work after four failed versions, and whether the CWM evaluation reveals a different pattern than what we saw with Qwen. These results will determine if the model-contingent narrative holds up—if both succeed and show divergent behaviors, that strengthens the core framing.\n\nIf DeepSeek works but CWM also fails like Qwen's did, the story shifts to emphasizing CLS as consistently safer at repo-level, which is less novel but still publishable, though EMNLP main becomes a stretch. The worst scenario is if DeepSeek's repo experiments collapse entirely like versions one through four, leaving us with only Qwen's results and function-level data to work with.\n\nNow I'm looking at what happens if we only have one model family at repo-level—that's a significant limitation for supporting the design space claim, so I'd need to reframe around the function-level analysis as the core contribution and position Qwen as a case study, or pivot toward the methodology itself as the novel contribution.\n\nLet me map out the concrete performance numbers that would determine which tier we're in: function-level gaps are already established at around half a percentage point for CLS versus CWM, with CLS showing a 2-3 percentage point advantage over trajectory-based approaches. For repo-level, the best case would have DeepSeek CLS hitting 80-85% accuracy while CWM stays competitive in the 75-82% range, whereas the worst case leaves us scrambling to justify the findings with incomplete data.\n\nThe narrative strategy depends heavily on which tier materializes—if results are strong across models, I can claim the design space is model-contingent with full characterization; if they're middling, I'd soften to saying CLS is the reliable default while CWM's viability depends on the model; if they're weak, I'd need to lean hard on the methodology contribution and the function-level null result as the actual finding.\n\nNow I'm reconsidering the tier predictions against what's actually running—the DeepSeek experiments are in various states, with some failed runs, one still analyzing, and the CWM variant having trained successfully at significant computational cost. This changes how optimistic I should be about the cross-model validation story. I need to see the next thinking to rewrite it. Could you provide the next thinking chunk that follows the current rewritten thinking?","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34399,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34399},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"999e06ea-df81-449b-a1e7-79420d02176f","uuid":"a69b24f1-2dbd-48b2-b3d9-088620b61df3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MgV6dBDbTYi5qT7GWtcBCA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"DeepSeek repo-level 实验全线跑通，且 CWM 在 DeepSeek 上表现与 CLS 持平或更优——直接验证 'formulation 优劣是 model-contingent' 的核心叙事\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"deepseek-cls-repo-v5 训练成功且 test acc ≥80%\"\n      - \"deepseek-cwm-repo eval unparseable rate <20%（vs Qwen 93%），acc 与 CLS 持平或反超\"\n      - \"Cross-model divergence 在 repo-level 清晰：Qwen CLS>>CWM, DeepSeek CWM≥CLS\"\n      - \"Func-level TOST equivalence 已锁定（p=0.007），无需额外实验\"\n      - \"DeepSeek TRAJ repo 8k 结果（75-81%）提供第三 formulation 的 repo-level 对比点\"\n    number_ranges:\n      deepseek_cls_repo_acc: [80, 86]\n      deepseek_cwm_repo_acc: [78, 85]\n      deepseek_cwm_repo_unparseable_pct: [5, 20]\n      qwen_cwm_repo_unparseable_pct: [90, 95]  # 已观测，锁定\n      func_level_cls_cwm_gap_pp: [-1.5, 1.0]  # 已观测，两个模型族均等价\n      repo_level_cross_model_reversal_pp: [3, 15]  # DeepSeek CWM minus CLS 减 Qwen CWM minus CLS\n      oracle_ensemble_gain_pp: [2, 4]\n      expected_reviewer_score: [3.5, 4.0]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Path B 完全成立。Title: \"The Formulation Design Space for Neural Code Verification\"。\n      Headline: 没有单一 formulation 普遍最优；func-level 三种等价，repo-level 优劣取决于 model/tokenizer。\n      最强 novelty: CWM 在 Qwen 上 93% unparseable 但在 DeepSeek 上 <20%——证明失败是 tokenizer-specific 而非 formulation-inherent。\n      Complementarity + efficiency（6-9x）作为实用 takeaway。\n      Claims 无需降级，所有 5 个 core findings 均有 cross-model 数据支撑。\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"DeepSeek repo-level CLS 勉强跑通但 CWM 仍然高 unparseable（与 Qwen 相似模式），cross-model 'reversal' 叙事不成立，退守为 'CLS 是 robust default'\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"deepseek-cls-repo-v5 训练成功但 acc 75-82%（噪音大，test set 小 n≈48-100）\"\n      - \"deepseek-cwm-repo eval unparseable rate 40-70%——比 Qwen 好但仍不可用\"\n      - \"Cross-model divergence 存在但方向一致（两个模型族都是 CLS > CWM at repo-level）\"\n      - \"DeepSeek TRAJ repo 提供补充数据点但 test set 太小（n=48）无法做 significance test\"\n      - \"Func-level equivalence + repo-level 'CLS dominates' 是可发表但 predictable 的结论\"\n    number_ranges:\n      deepseek_cls_repo_acc: [75, 82]\n      deepseek_cwm_repo_acc: [55, 70]\n      deepseek_cwm_repo_unparseable_pct: [40, 70]\n      func_level_cls_cwm_gap_pp: [-1.5, 1.0]  # 已锁定\n      repo_cls_vs_cwm_gap_consistent_pp: [5, 20]  # 两个模型族方向一致\n      expected_reviewer_score: [3.0, 3.5]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Path A 成立但 novelty 削弱。Framing 调整为: \"CLS is the robust formulation at repo-level;\n      CWM generation fails at scale due to tokenizer-dependent format compliance, but the\n      severity varies across model families (93% vs ~50% unparseable).\" \n      Claim 2 (model-contingent divergence) 弱化为 \"degree of CWM failure is model-dependent\"\n      而非 \"which formulation wins is model-dependent\"。\n      需要加强 complementarity analysis 和 efficiency argument 来弥补 novelty gap。\n      补充实验建议: (1) CWM constrained decoding ablation 证明 parsing 是瓶颈; \n      (2) 加入 process-vs-outcome supervision 的 Related Work section 强化 NLP 社区 relevance。\n      EMNLP main borderline，Findings 有把握。\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"DeepSeek repo-level 全部失败（延续 v1-v4 的 pattern），只有 Qwen 单模型族的 repo-level 数据，cross-model 验证仅限 func-level\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"deepseek-cls-repo-v5 训练失败或 acc ≤ majority baseline（~73%）\"\n      - \"deepseek-cwm-repo eval 不可用（crash、unparseable >80%、或 acc 远低于 baseline）\"\n      - \"Repo-level 结论完全依赖 Qwen 单模型族——reviewer 会质疑 generalizability\"\n      - \"DeepSeek TRAJ repo 是唯一跑通的 DeepSeek repo-level 实验，但 n=48 太小\"\n      - \"Func-level 双模型族数据完整且 clean，但 repo-level 是 paper 的 differentiator\"\n    number_ranges:\n      deepseek_cls_repo_acc: [50, 73]  # 不超过 majority baseline\n      deepseek_cwm_repo_acc: [40, 60]  # 严重失败\n      deepseek_cwm_repo_unparseable_pct: [70, 95]\n      qwen_cls_repo_best_acc: [83, 86]  # 已有数据，锁定\n      qwen_cwm_repo_best_parseable_acc: [42, 58]  # 已观测\n      func_level_all_formulations_acc_range: [83, 90]  # 已锁定，两模型族\n      expected_reviewer_score: [2.5, 3.0]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      核心 reframe: 放弃 repo-level 作为 main contribution，转为 secondary finding。\n      新 angle 选项 (仍冲 EMNLP main):\n      (1) \"Per-Test vs Trajectory-Level Verification: A Controlled Study\" — 将 CLS vs TRAJ 的\n      粒度-效率 tradeoff 提为核心贡献（双模型族 func-level 数据完整 + Qwen repo-level 作 case study）。\n      强调 per-test 在 accuracy 不损失前提下提供 diagnostic granularity + 6-9x speedup。\n      TOST equivalence p=0.007 是 solid statistical result。\n      (2) Block-correlation empirical validation (ICC=0.19, design effect=4.0) 作为 methodological\n      contribution——揭示 per-test evaluation 中 i.i.d. 假设不成立的系统性偏差。\n      (3) CWM repo-level failure analysis 降为一个 section 而非 core claim，explicitly scope\n      为 \"Qwen3 case study, cross-model validation as future work\"。\n      Re-repair negative result 诚实报告为 future work motivation。\n      Efficiency + diagnostic granularity + statistical methodology 三条线撑起 paper。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34399,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34399},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"999e06ea-df81-449b-a1e7-79420d02176f","uuid":"b381edcd-cb41-4908-8754-caac03658a9e"}
